From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:25:06 +0000
Subject: fix(compose): catch up text committed at blur before clearing focus

Dictation and some IME paths only commit text when the editor resigns
first responder. When the blur event carries a "text" key (new
InputParams.hasText), CoreTextField now pushes that value through the same
recordNativeValue + onValueChange path before clearing focus. iOS
KRTextAreaView sends the raw output text (attachments restored, via the
new KRTextBlurEventPayload helper) instead of the display string. Also sets
hasText on TextAreaEvent.inputBlur, which Compose TextFields bind to;
without it the catch-up never ran (fork #163 only set it on InputEvent).

Fork-Patch: input-blur-text-catchup
Origin: db77397b (+ hasText fix for TextAreaEvent.inputBlur)
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

diff --git a/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/foundation/text/CoreTextField.kt b/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/foundation/text/CoreTextField.kt
index 3468742af256bc8d39e00a55145df1a2e9f1c510..9d24563a5877ec31ff34061ff65c8b262daf9342 100644
--- a/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/foundation/text/CoreTextField.kt
+++ b/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/foundation/text/CoreTextField.kt
@@ -415,6 +415,22 @@ internal fun CoreTextField(
         }
     }
     val inputBlurEvent: InputEventHandlerFn = updatedNodeEvent { params ->
+        // Dictation (and other IME paths) may only commit their text at blur time:
+        // iOS textViewDidEndEditing attaches the final textView.text to this event.
+        // If we only cleared focus here, that committed text would never reach
+        // onValueChange and the draft would stay empty. Catch the value up first
+        // when the event actually carries text; platforms whose blur event has no
+        // text key (hasText == false) are completely untouched.
+        if (params.hasText && params.text != lastSyncedTextInputState?.text) {
+            val blurValue = TextFieldValue(
+                text = params.text,
+                selection = TextRange(params.text.length),
+            )
+            lastSyncedTextInputState = TextInputState(text = params.text)
+            autoHeightTextAreaView.getViewAttr().updatePropCache(TextConst.VALUE, params.text)
+            controlledStateArbiter.recordNativeValue(blurValue)
+            onValueChange(blurValue)
+        }
         if (
             kuiklyKeyboardController?.onNativeBlur(
                 autoHeightTextAreaView,
